L0200: Name does not denote a type

A name in a type position resolves to a value-producing declaration instead of a type. A function name cannot be used as the type of its return value. Use the declared data type or a supported logical callable signature.

Example from `tests/corpus/reject/function_as_type.lc`; the full file is a regression test.

```locus
// A function's name where a type is needed.
fn double(n: u8) -> u8 { n.wrapping_add(n) }

fn first(n: double) -> u8 { 1 }
```

Language, as built: [1.3:1](../../atlas.html#/doc/language/spec-1.3:1).
